1
00:00:01,919 --> 00:00:03,170
WHY IS EVERYBODY USING

2
00:00:03,211 --> 00:00:04,839
THESE TINY LITTLE LIGHTS
NOWADAYS?

3
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:07,132
I REMEMBER WHEN PEOPLE
USED TO USE BIG LIGHTS.

4
00:00:07,174 --> 00:00:09,844
THAT'S A GOOD
STORY, GRANDPA.

5
00:00:11,094 --> 00:00:12,888
HEY.

6
00:00:12,930 --> 00:00:14,348
All:
HEY.

7
00:00:14,389 --> 00:00:15,975
WOW.

8
00:00:16,015 --> 00:00:18,018
MONICA'S LETTING OTHER PEOPLE
HELP DECORATE HER TREE.

9
00:00:18,059 --> 00:00:20,187
DID SOMEONE
GET HER DRUNK AGAIN?

10
00:00:21,355 --> 00:00:23,398
HAVING A PERFECTLY
DECORATED TREE

11
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:24,984
IS NOT WHAT
CHRISTMAS IS ABOUT.

12
00:00:25,024 --> 00:00:27,068
IT'S ABOUT BEING WITH
THE PEOPLE YOU LOVE.

13
00:00:27,110 --> 00:00:28,320
THAT IS NICE

14
00:00:28,362 --> 00:00:29,738
AND WE'RE DONE, TA-DA!

15
00:00:30,865 --> 00:00:32,783
Chandler:
I DON'T KNOW WHAT IT IS.

16
00:00:32,825 --> 00:00:35,160
IT JUST DOESN'T QUITE FEEL
LIKE CHRISTMAS TO ME.

17
00:00:35,202 --> 00:00:37,204
OH, YEAH.

18
00:00:40,332 --> 00:00:42,710
NOW IT FEELS
LIKE CHRISTMAS.

19
00:00:49,550 --> 00:00:54,972
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

20
00:00:55,014 --> 00:00:57,182
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

21
00:00:57,224 --> 00:00:59,434
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

22
00:00:59,476 --> 00:01:04,439
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

23
00:01:04,481 --> 00:01:06,692
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

24
00:01:06,734 --> 00:01:10,029
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

25
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:13,198
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

26
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:16,535
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

27
00:01:24,376 --> 00:01:27,046
AND THAT'S THE STORY
OF THE DREIDEL.

28
00:01:29,006 --> 00:01:31,341
NOW, SOME PEOPLE TRACE
THE CHRISTMAS TREE

29
00:01:31,383 --> 00:01:32,801
BACK TO THE EGYPTIANS

30
00:01:32,843 --> 00:01:35,303
WHO USED TO BRING
GREEN PALM BRANCHES

31
00:01:35,345 --> 00:01:38,306
INTO THEIR HUTS
ON THE SHORTEST DAY OF THE YEAR

32
00:01:38,348 --> 00:01:41,142
SYMBOLIZING LIFE'S TRIUMPH
OVER DEATH

33
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:43,979
AND THAT WAS, LIKE,
4,000 YEARS AGO.

34
00:01:44,021 --> 00:01:45,981
SO PRETTY MUCH
AROUND THE SAME TIME

35
00:01:46,023 --> 00:01:47,858
YOU STARTED TELLING THIS STORY.

36
00:01:50,402 --> 00:01:51,570
HEY, YOU GUYS.

37
00:01:51,612 --> 00:01:52,780
HEY, JOE,
WHAT'S UP?

38
00:01:52,821 --> 00:01:54,949
I HAD TO GET OUT
OF THE APARTMENT.

39
00:01:54,990 --> 00:01:57,993
JANINE IS, LIKE,
STRETCHING ALL OVER THE PLACE.

40
00:01:58,035 --> 00:01:59,995
EVERYWHERE I LOOK,
SHE'S, LIKE...

41
00:02:04,291 --> 00:02:07,127
I CAN SEE WHY THAT'S
HARD TO RESIST.

42
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:09,504
I LIKE HER SO MUCH!

43
00:02:09,546 --> 00:02:10,839
I'M SORRY, SWEETIE

44
00:02:10,881 --> 00:02:12,466
THAT SHE DOESN'T FEEL
THE SAME WAY.

45
00:02:12,507 --> 00:02:14,009
SHE'S SO SWEET.

46
00:02:14,051 --> 00:02:17,763
I JUST WANT TO FEED HER GRAPES
AND BRUSH HER HAIR.

47
00:02:17,805 --> 00:02:21,100
YOU ARE AWARE THAT SHE'S
NOT A MONKEY, RIGHT?

48
00:02:22,726 --> 00:02:26,730
I AM SO OVER JANINE.

49
00:02:26,772 --> 00:02:28,231
I MEAN...

50
00:02:28,273 --> 00:02:30,150
AT FIRST, I THOUGHT SHE WAS HOT

51
00:02:30,191 --> 00:02:32,444
BUT NOW, SHE'S LIKE, OLD NEWS.

52
00:02:32,486 --> 00:02:33,570
HI, GUYS.

53
00:02:33,612 --> 00:02:35,155
JANINE!

54
00:02:35,196 --> 00:02:36,573
COFFEE TO GO, PLEASE.

55
00:02:36,615 --> 00:02:38,993
I JUST GOT A CALL
TO BE A DANCER

56
00:02:39,034 --> 00:02:41,578
ON A TELEVISION SPECIAL
FOR NEW YEAR'S EVE.

57
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:45,165
IT'S CALLED SOME SORT OF
"DICKIN' ROCKIN' DICKIE EVE."

58
00:02:47,042 --> 00:02:48,502
HOLD IT.

59
00:02:48,543 --> 00:02:50,587
ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT

60
00:02:50,629 --> 00:02:53,548
DICK CLARK'S
NEW YEAR'S ROCKIN' EVE?

61
00:02:53,590 --> 00:02:54,716
YEAH. THAT'S WHAT I SAID.

62
00:02:57,385 --> 00:02:59,054
OH, MY GOD!

63
00:02:59,096 --> 00:03:00,681
WE LOVE THAT SHOW.

64
00:03:00,722 --> 00:03:02,516
ROSS AND I HAVE
BEEN WATCHING IT

65
00:03:02,557 --> 00:03:04,309
SINCE I CAN REMEMBER.

66
00:03:04,351 --> 00:03:06,895
YOU'RE STILL JUST
A LITTLE FAT GIRL INSIDE

67
00:03:06,937 --> 00:03:08,313
AREN'T YOU?

68
00:03:09,857 --> 00:03:11,232
I'LL BE ON IT THIS YEAR.

69
00:03:11,274 --> 00:03:12,693
I'LL BE ONE
OF THE PARTY PEOPLE.

70
00:03:12,734 --> 00:03:14,820
YOU'RE GOING TO BE
A PARTY PERSON?!

71
00:03:14,862 --> 00:03:17,948
THOSE GUYS ROCK THE MOST!

72
00:03:17,990 --> 00:03:19,908
THEY SAID I SHOULD
BRING SOMEONE.

73
00:03:19,950 --> 00:03:21,535
DO YOU WANT TO BE
MY DANCE PARTNER?

74
00:03:21,576 --> 00:03:22,828
TOTALLY!

75
00:03:22,870 --> 00:03:24,496
I WOULD LOVE TO SPEND
NEW YEAR'S WITH YOU.

76
00:03:24,538 --> 00:03:26,205
ACTUALLY, THEY'RE TAPING
TOMORROW.

77
00:03:26,247 --> 00:03:27,499
I DON'T REALLY
UNDERSTAND WHY.

78
00:03:27,541 --> 00:03:29,208
HOW IT WORKS IS

79
00:03:29,250 --> 00:03:31,378
THE PART WITH DICK CLARK
IN TIMES SQUARE

80
00:03:31,419 --> 00:03:32,880
IS ACTUALLY LIVE

81
00:03:32,921 --> 00:03:36,633
BUT THEY TAPE SOME OF
THE PARTY STUFF AHEAD OF TIME.

82
00:03:36,675 --> 00:03:39,094
NOT A LOT OF PEOPLE KNOW THAT.

83
00:03:40,179 --> 00:03:42,181
DO YOU GUYS
WANT TO COME, TOO?

84
00:03:42,221 --> 00:03:43,974
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

85
00:03:44,016 --> 00:03:46,226
WE ARE THERE.

86
00:03:46,267 --> 00:03:49,188
( laughing )

87
00:03:49,228 --> 00:03:51,231
WHAT ARE YOU
LAUGHING AT?

88
00:03:51,272 --> 00:03:53,441
WELL, I USED TO DATE HIM

89
00:03:53,483 --> 00:03:55,443
BUT YOU'RE STILL
GOING OUT WITH HER.

90
00:03:57,738 --> 00:03:58,906
OH, THANKS.

91
00:03:58,947 --> 00:04:01,324
GREAT. SO WE CAN
ALL GO TOGETHER.

92
00:04:01,366 --> 00:04:03,118
WELL, I'LL
CATCH YOU LATER.

93
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:04,995
BYE, JANINE.

94
00:04:06,788 --> 00:04:09,583
DID SHE JUST ASK ME OUT
ON A DATE?

95
00:04:09,624 --> 00:04:12,669
I DON'T THINK SO.

96
00:04:12,711 --> 00:04:14,295
SHE JUST INVITED HIM TO

97
00:04:14,337 --> 00:04:16,255
THE BIGGEST PARTY
OF THE MILLENNIUM.

98
00:04:16,297 --> 00:04:18,466
YEAH, BUT SHE ALSO INVITED
YOU AND ROSS.

99
00:04:18,508 --> 00:04:19,968
HONEY, I'M SORRY

100
00:04:20,010 --> 00:04:22,429
BUT I DON'T THINK THAT WAS
A ROMANTIC THING.

101
00:04:22,470 --> 00:04:24,723
I KNOW HOW I CAN FIND OUT.

102
00:04:24,765 --> 00:04:27,350
WE'RE GOING TO A NEW YEAR'S EVE
PARTY, RIGHT?

103
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:29,477
AT MIDNIGHT, I CAN KISS HER.

104
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:31,855
IF SHE KISSES ME BACK, GREAT.

105
00:04:31,897 --> 00:04:35,650
BUT IF SHE SAYS, "DUDE,
WHAT THE HELL ARE YOU DOING?"

106
00:04:35,692 --> 00:04:38,612
I CAN SAY, "IT WASN'T ME;
IT WAS NEW YEAR'S."

107
00:04:39,988 --> 00:04:43,700
THAT'S A LOT BETTER THAN ROSS
TRYING TO KISS ME IN HIGH SCHOOL

108
00:04:43,742 --> 00:04:47,037
AND SAYING THAT HE DID IT
BECAUSE HE NEEDED CHAPSTICK.

109
00:04:47,079 --> 00:04:50,958
IT WAS A DRY DAY.

110
00:04:54,128 --> 00:04:55,921
WE ARE GOING TO

111
00:04:55,963 --> 00:04:59,216
DICK CLARK'S NEW YEAR'S
ROCKIN' EVE!

112
00:04:59,258 --> 00:05:00,842
OH, MY GOD!

113
00:05:00,884 --> 00:05:03,053
OH, MY GOD!

114
00:05:03,095 --> 00:05:05,264
OH, MY GOD.

115
00:05:13,105 --> 00:05:14,064
OKAY, NOW LISTEN UP.

116
00:05:14,106 --> 00:05:15,149
I'VE BEEN ON SETS BEFORE.

117
00:05:15,190 --> 00:05:16,566
LET ME GIVE YOU
A LITTLE ADVICE.

118
00:05:16,608 --> 00:05:18,777
IT'S A SHOW,
BUT WE'RE JUST DANCING.

119
00:05:18,819 --> 00:05:19,945
IT'S NO BIG DEAL.

120
00:05:19,987 --> 00:05:21,655
THE IMPORTANT THING
TO REMEMBER:

121
00:05:21,696 --> 00:05:22,739
STAY COOL.

122
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:24,324
GOT IT.

123
00:05:24,365 --> 00:05:28,703
OH, MY GOD,
IT'S JUST LIKE I DREAMED IT!

124
00:05:29,871 --> 00:05:31,330
OKAY, EVERYONE, GATHER UP.

125
00:05:31,372 --> 00:05:32,833
Monica:
EXCUSE US.

126
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:35,210
EXCUSE US.

127
00:05:35,252 --> 00:05:36,670
HERE'S WHAT'S
GOING TO HAPPEN.

128
00:05:36,711 --> 00:05:38,379
THE MUSIC WILL START,
YOU'LL DANCE.

129
00:05:38,421 --> 00:05:40,465
WE'LL TAPE YOU;
DON'T LOOK AT THE CAMERA.

130
00:05:40,507 --> 00:05:41,466
ANY QUESTIONS?

131
00:05:41,508 --> 00:05:43,010
YEAH, I HAVE A QUESTION.

132
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:44,845
WHEN IS THIS
GOING TO AIR?

133
00:05:46,221 --> 00:05:47,346
YEAH.

134
00:05:47,388 --> 00:05:49,432
NOW, YOU GUYS,
DANCE OVER THERE.

135
00:05:49,474 --> 00:05:50,600
YOU GUYS, OVER THERE.

136
00:05:50,642 --> 00:05:52,393
I WANT YOU TWO
RIGHT AROUND HERE.

137
00:05:52,435 --> 00:05:53,728
EVERYONE ELSE, SPREAD OUT.

138
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:55,022
ROSS.

139
00:05:55,063 --> 00:05:58,483
SO WHEN IS IT
GOING TO AIR?

140
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:04,698
OKAY, PHEEBS, YOU LOOK
IN THE KITCHEN.

141
00:06:04,739 --> 00:06:06,116
I WILL LOOK
IN THE BACK CLOSET.

142
00:06:06,158 --> 00:06:07,492
I CAN SAVE YOU TIME, LADIES.

143
00:06:07,534 --> 00:06:09,703
I'M RIGHT HERE.

144
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:10,954
YEAH.

145
00:06:10,996 --> 00:06:13,040
CHANDLER, WHY DON'T YOU
TAKE A WALK?

146
00:06:13,081 --> 00:06:14,541
THIS DOESN'T CONCERN YOU.

147
00:06:14,582 --> 00:06:15,876
WE ARE LOOKING FOR

148
00:06:15,917 --> 00:06:17,878
OUR CHRISTMAS PRESENTS
FROM MONICA.

149
00:06:17,919 --> 00:06:19,629
WHAT? THAT'S TERRIBLE.

150
00:06:19,671 --> 00:06:21,506
NO, WE DO IT
EVERY YEAR.

151
00:06:21,548 --> 00:06:24,176
OH, WELL, THAT MAKES IT
NOT TERRIBLE.

152
00:06:24,218 --> 00:06:26,970
NO, YEAH. WE NEVER FIND THEM.

153
00:06:27,012 --> 00:06:31,308
SHE'S ALWAYS BESTED US,
THAT WILY... MINX.

154
00:06:31,350 --> 00:06:32,726
DON'T WORRY.

155
00:06:32,767 --> 00:06:34,728
WE'RE JUST GOING TO SEARCH HERE
FOR AN HOUR

156
00:06:34,769 --> 00:06:37,064
AND THEN WE'LL GO OVER TO JOEY'S
AND SEARCH, OKAY?

157
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:38,397
NO, NOT OKAY.

158
00:06:38,439 --> 00:06:39,691
YOU CAN'T LOOK FOR
MONICA'S PRESENTS.

159
00:06:39,733 --> 00:06:40,775
WE HAVE TO.

160
00:06:40,817 --> 00:06:43,195
YOU DON'T HAVE TO,
AND YOU CAN'T

161
00:06:43,237 --> 00:06:45,613
BECAUSE I LIVE HERE, TOO.

162
00:06:45,655 --> 00:06:48,909
WELL, THEN, YOU SHOULD
LOOK WITH US.

163
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:50,618
WHY?

164
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:53,412
AREN'T YOU WORRIED
ABOUT WHAT TO GET
MONICA FOR CHRISTMAS?

165
00:06:53,454 --> 00:06:55,874
I HAVE A GREAT IDEA
FOR A PRESENT FOR HER.

166
00:06:55,916 --> 00:06:59,086
( scoffing ):
THAT'S IT, "A GREAT IDEA"?

167
00:06:59,127 --> 00:07:00,628
CHANDLER,
THAT'S NOT ENOUGH.

168
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:02,505
WHAT IF SHE GETS YOU
A GREAT PRESENT

169
00:07:02,547 --> 00:07:03,631
TWO MEDIUM PRESENTS

170
00:07:03,673 --> 00:07:05,384
AND THEN A BUNCH
OF LITTLE PRESENTS

171
00:07:05,424 --> 00:07:07,426
AND YOU'VE JUST GOTTEN HER
ONE GREAT PRESENT?

172
00:07:07,468 --> 00:07:08,427
THAT'S JUST GOING TO
MAKE HER FEEL BAD.

173
00:07:08,469 --> 00:07:09,428
WHY WOULD YOU

174
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:11,472
DO THAT TO
HER, CHANDLER?

175
00:07:13,141 --> 00:07:14,226
IF I HELPED

176
00:07:14,268 --> 00:07:15,560
WE COULD FIND THEM FASTER.

177
00:07:15,602 --> 00:07:16,770
THAT'S RIGHT.

178
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:19,356
OOH, WE HAVE A LIVE ONE.

179
00:07:19,398 --> 00:07:20,774
IT'S A MACY'S BAG.

180
00:07:20,815 --> 00:07:22,234
YEAH.

181
00:07:22,276 --> 00:07:24,861
OOH, WHO'S IT FOR?

182
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:28,823
"DEAR LOSERS, DO YOU
REALLY THINK

183
00:07:28,865 --> 00:07:31,534
I'D HIDE PRESENTS
UNDER THE COUCH?"

184
00:07:32,953 --> 00:07:35,580
"P.S.: CHANDLER, I KNEW
THEY'D BREAK YOU."

185
00:07:38,750 --> 00:07:41,586
UH-OH. SHE MAY BE ON TO US.

186
00:07:41,628 --> 00:07:44,631
WE ARE SO GOING TO FIND THEM
THIS YEAR.

187
00:07:44,672 --> 00:07:45,882
YOU SAID YOU WERE

188
00:07:45,924 --> 00:07:47,968
GOING ACROSS THE
HALL AND LOOK.

189
00:07:48,009 --> 00:07:49,719
YOU DON'T DO THAT
EVERY YEAR, DO YOU?

190
00:07:49,761 --> 00:07:50,762
YEAH.

191
00:07:50,804 --> 00:07:51,846
YOU DON'T, LIKE

192
00:07:51,888 --> 00:07:53,974
GO INTO THE BACK
OF MY CLOSET

193
00:07:54,015 --> 00:07:56,310
AND LOOK UNDER
MY GYM BAG OR ANYTHING.

194
00:07:57,894 --> 00:07:59,520
NO. WE NEVER DO THAT.

195
00:08:01,522 --> 00:08:04,484
BECAUSE THAT'S WHERE JOEY
GAVE ME SOME STUFF TO STORE

196
00:08:04,525 --> 00:08:05,777
THAT I'VE NEVER

197
00:08:05,819 --> 00:08:08,155
SEEN BEFORE
IN MY LIFE.

198
00:08:08,196 --> 00:08:10,782
OKAY, THAT DID NOT JUST HAPPEN.

199
00:08:18,415 --> 00:08:20,292
OKAY, HERE COMES
ANOTHER CAMERA.

200
00:08:20,334 --> 00:08:22,501
RIGHT. NO BIGGIE;
STAY LOOSE.

201
00:08:31,761 --> 00:08:33,805
WHY DO THEY
KEEP DOING THAT?

202
00:08:33,847 --> 00:08:35,807
IF WE WANT TO GET ON CAMERA

203
00:08:35,849 --> 00:08:37,809
WE HAVE TO GET ON
ONE OF THOSE PLATFORMS.

204
00:08:37,851 --> 00:08:39,811
THEY'VE BEEN TAPING
THOSE PEOPLE ALL DAY.

205
00:08:39,853 --> 00:08:41,520
RIGHT.

206
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:48,403
HEY, WHAT DID YOU GUYS DO
TO GET UP ON THERE?

207
00:08:48,445 --> 00:08:50,197
WE LEARNED HOW TO DANCE.

208
00:08:50,238 --> 00:08:51,239
OH, YEAH?

209
00:08:51,281 --> 00:08:53,158
WHEN YOU LEARNED
HOW TO DANCE

210
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:55,243
DID YOU FORGET HOW TO
PUT ON UNDERPANTS?

211
00:08:55,285 --> 00:08:56,286
YEAH.

212
00:08:59,956 --> 00:09:02,376
HEY, YOU'RE
A GOOD DANCER.

213
00:09:02,417 --> 00:09:03,835
REALLY?

214
00:09:03,877 --> 00:09:06,046
YOU'D BE BETTER IF YOU
LOOSENED YOUR HIPS A LITTLE.

215
00:09:06,087 --> 00:09:07,130
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

216
00:09:07,172 --> 00:09:08,756
WELL, LIKE THIS.

217
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:12,052
THAT'S IT.

218
00:09:12,093 --> 00:09:13,220
JUST FEEL THE RHYTHM.

219
00:09:13,261 --> 00:09:14,513
THAT'S BETTER.

220
00:09:14,554 --> 00:09:17,224
( falsetto ):
UH-HUH.

221
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:18,892
YOU'RE DANCING
WITH THAT GIRL THERE.

222
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:20,185
NO, NO, NO.

223
00:09:20,227 --> 00:09:21,686
WE CAME TOGETHER.

224
00:09:21,728 --> 00:09:23,271
I DON'T SEE IT.

225
00:09:23,313 --> 00:09:25,857
YOU ARE DANCING WITH
THE TALL GUY OVER THERE.

226
00:09:25,899 --> 00:09:27,901
TALL GUY,
RAISE YOUR HAND.

227
00:09:30,611 --> 00:09:31,863
PLEASE LET ME
DANCE WITH THAT GIRL.

228
00:09:31,905 --> 00:09:33,114
I REALLY LIKE HER

229
00:09:33,156 --> 00:09:33,990
AND I THINK I
HAVE A SHOT.

230
00:09:34,032 --> 00:09:36,451
REALLY? YOU THINK SO?
I DON'T.

231
00:09:53,301 --> 00:09:54,886
I COULDN'T FIND ANYTHING
AT JOEY...

232
00:09:54,928 --> 00:09:55,929
HEY, WHOA, WHOA.

233
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:57,889
WE FOUND THEM.

234
00:09:57,931 --> 00:10:00,392
THEY WERE IN THE GUEST ROOM
CLOSET BEHIND SOME COATS.

235
00:10:00,434 --> 00:10:02,310
YEAH, AND YOU HAVE
NOTHING TO WORRY ABOUT

236
00:10:02,352 --> 00:10:03,520
'CAUSE THEY'RE ALL CRAP.

237
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:06,940
THOSE ARE MY GIFTS.

238
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:08,400
I GOT THOSE FOR YOU.

239
00:10:10,818 --> 00:10:12,779
OH, THANKS, CHANDLER.

240
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:14,114
THEY'RE GREAT.

241
00:10:14,155 --> 00:10:16,032
Rachel:
WELL, CHANDLER

242
00:10:16,074 --> 00:10:19,619
THEN WHAT IS THIS VERY
WEIRD METAL "A," "Z" THING?

243
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:21,246
THOSE ARE BOOKENDS.

244
00:10:21,288 --> 00:10:22,956
THAT'S A GREAT GIFT.

245
00:10:22,997 --> 00:10:24,665
OH, OKAY, I'M SORRY.

246
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:26,667
THANK YOU FOR MY "AZ."

247
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:32,090
MAKE SURE YOU PUT ALL THAT STUFF
BACK IN THE CLOSET, OKAY?

248
00:10:32,132 --> 00:10:33,632
YES, OKAY.

249
00:10:33,674 --> 00:10:35,469
OH, BY THE WAY,
I JUST GOT TO SAY

250
00:10:35,510 --> 00:10:38,888
I THINK IT'S REALLY NICE OF YOU
THAT EVEN AFTER YOU'VE MOVED

251
00:10:38,930 --> 00:10:41,349
YOU STILL KEEP STORING
THAT STUFF FOR JOEY.

252
00:10:56,906 --> 00:10:58,950
HEY, DANCING GIRL.

253
00:10:58,992 --> 00:11:02,412
CAN I... CAN I GO
TO THE BATHROOM?

254
00:11:03,704 --> 00:11:05,373
OKAY, HERE WE GO.

255
00:11:05,415 --> 00:11:07,375
YEAH. THERE YOU GO.

256
00:11:11,421 --> 00:11:13,381
LOOKING GOOD, GELLERS.

257
00:11:13,423 --> 00:11:16,134
WE KNOW.

258
00:11:16,176 --> 00:11:17,302
HEY, LOOK.

259
00:11:17,344 --> 00:11:18,761
YOU KNOW THAT
SNIPPY GUY OVER THERE?

260
00:11:18,803 --> 00:11:21,014
HE'S THE ONE WHO DECIDES
WHO GETS ON THE PLATFORM.

261
00:11:21,055 --> 00:11:22,182
WE SHOULD GO
DANCE BY HIM.

262
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:23,350
OKAY.

263
00:11:30,982 --> 00:11:32,733
OKAY, EVERYBODY HOLD.

264
00:11:34,693 --> 00:11:37,572
NEXT ON THE
PLATFORMS ARE...

265
00:11:41,576 --> 00:11:43,537
YOU TWO.

266
00:11:43,578 --> 00:11:45,079
AND...

267
00:11:46,581 --> 00:11:48,375
YOU TWO.

268
00:11:48,416 --> 00:11:49,917
EXCUSE ME, SIR.

269
00:11:49,959 --> 00:11:52,420
WOULD IT HELP IF I WEREN'T
WEARING UNDERPANTS?

270
00:11:52,462 --> 00:11:54,005
MONICA!

271
00:11:54,047 --> 00:11:55,340
WOULD IT?

272
00:12:02,347 --> 00:12:05,308
HEY, TALL GUY.

273
00:12:05,350 --> 00:12:08,228
LISTEN, I WANT TO TALK
TO YOU ABOUT THAT GIRL

274
00:12:08,269 --> 00:12:09,854
THAT YOU'RE
DANCING WITH.

275
00:12:09,896 --> 00:12:11,147
SHE'S NICE, HUH?

276
00:12:11,189 --> 00:12:13,732
TO THINK I ALMOST
BROUGHT MY WIFE TO THIS.

277
00:12:13,774 --> 00:12:16,777
YEAH, YEAH. OKAY.

278
00:12:19,447 --> 00:12:21,908
UH, LOOK, BUDDY,
I CAME WITH THAT GIRL.

279
00:12:21,949 --> 00:12:23,660
AND I HAD THIS PLAN
TO KISS HER

280
00:12:23,702 --> 00:12:25,245
AT THE NEW YEAR'S
COUNTDOWN.

281
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:26,413
I'M TRYING TO WIN HER OVER,
YOU KNOW?

282
00:12:26,454 --> 00:12:27,664
SO I WAS WONDERING...

283
00:12:27,706 --> 00:12:29,249
I DON'T THINK SO.

284
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:30,500
OH, COME ON, MAN.

285
00:12:30,542 --> 00:12:31,668
YOU CAN DANCE
WITH MY PARTNER.

286
00:12:31,710 --> 00:12:34,045
SHE'S REAL MELLOW.

287
00:12:34,087 --> 00:12:37,424
LOOK, YOU DATING THIS
GIRL YOU CAME WITH?

288
00:12:37,465 --> 00:12:39,217
WELL, I WAS HOPING
AFTER TONIGHT

289
00:12:39,259 --> 00:12:40,427
THAT MAYBE I COULD...

290
00:12:40,468 --> 00:12:43,388
NO, NO, SHE'S FAIR GAME
IF YOU ASK ME.

291
00:12:43,430 --> 00:12:44,431
SORRY, BUDDY.

292
00:12:44,472 --> 00:12:46,140
ALL RIGHT.

293
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:47,601
HEY, YOU KNOW,
FAIR IS FAIR.

294
00:12:47,642 --> 00:12:49,561
I MEAN, WHEN YOU'RE
RIGHT YOU'RE RIGHT.

295
00:12:49,603 --> 00:12:50,769
WHAT CAN I SAY, BUT...

296
00:12:50,811 --> 00:12:53,314
HEY!

297
00:12:53,356 --> 00:12:54,857
GOD!

298
00:12:54,899 --> 00:12:56,693
WHAT, ARE YOU IN
THE SECOND GRADE?

299
00:12:56,735 --> 00:12:59,362
HEY, MAN, YOU'RE THE ONE
WHO WET HIS PANTS.

300
00:12:59,404 --> 00:13:00,905
HEY! HEY!

301
00:13:00,947 --> 00:13:02,073
HEY!

302
00:13:06,494 --> 00:13:08,955
MAN, THIS SUCKS.

303
00:13:08,996 --> 00:13:10,707
IF MOM AND DAD DON'T
SEE US ON TV

304
00:13:10,749 --> 00:13:12,250
AFTER WE MADE THEM
SO JEALOUS

305
00:13:12,292 --> 00:13:14,085
WHO'S GOING TO BE
THE LOSERS THEN?

306
00:13:16,087 --> 00:13:19,466
HEY, I KNOW WHAT WILL GET
US UP ON A PLATFORM.

307
00:13:19,507 --> 00:13:20,508
WHAT?

308
00:13:20,550 --> 00:13:22,801
THE ROUTINE.

309
00:13:22,843 --> 00:13:27,223
ROSS, WE HAVEN'T DONE
THE ROUTINE SINCE MIDDLE SCHOOL.

310
00:13:27,265 --> 00:13:29,850
HEY, WHEN THE SNIPPY GUY
SEES THE ROUTINE

311
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:32,562
HE'LL WANT TO BUILD US
OUR OWN PLATFORM.

312
00:13:32,604 --> 00:13:34,063
WAS IT REALLY THAT GOOD?

313
00:13:34,105 --> 00:13:35,607
WE GOT HONORABLE MENTION

314
00:13:35,649 --> 00:13:37,942
IN THE BROTHER/SISTER
DANCE CATEGORY.

315
00:13:37,984 --> 00:13:39,860
LOOK, IT'S ALMOST
FAKE MIDNIGHT.

316
00:13:39,902 --> 00:13:42,155
DO WE REALLY HAVE
ANY OTHER CHOICE?

317
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:45,492
OKAY, LET'S DO IT.

318
00:13:45,533 --> 00:13:48,077
MOM AND DAD ARE GOING
TO BE SO FACED.

319
00:13:55,042 --> 00:13:57,504
FIVE, SIX, SEVEN, EIGHT.

320
00:14:38,961 --> 00:14:41,130
SO, DO WE REALLY
NEED TO ASK

321
00:14:41,172 --> 00:14:44,050
WHO'S GOING UP ON
THE PLATFORM NEXT?

322
00:14:44,091 --> 00:14:45,468
OH, NO.

323
00:14:45,510 --> 00:14:47,261
GET UP THERE AND DO THAT
AGAIN EXACTLY LIKE THAT.

324
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:48,638
YEAH!

325
00:14:50,014 --> 00:14:51,641
MAKE SURE AND GET THIS.

326
00:14:51,683 --> 00:14:54,519
DICK WILL WANT IT
FOR THE BLOOPERS SHOW.

327
00:14:54,561 --> 00:14:55,729
ALL RIGHT, CUT.

328
00:14:55,770 --> 00:14:56,813
LISTEN UP, EVERYONE.

329
00:14:56,855 --> 00:14:58,147
WHEN WE START AGAIN

330
00:14:58,189 --> 00:15:00,316
IT'S GOING TO BE THE
COUNTDOWN TO NEW YEAR'S

331
00:15:00,358 --> 00:15:03,653
SO I WANT TO SEE
EVERYBODY'S EXCITEMENT.

332
00:15:03,695 --> 00:15:06,030
HEY, GUY, YOU'VE GOT
ABOUT THREE SECONDS

333
00:15:06,072 --> 00:15:07,407
TO GET AWAY
FROM MY PARTNER.

334
00:15:07,448 --> 00:15:09,200
WHAT'S GOING ON
OVER HERE?

335
00:15:09,242 --> 00:15:11,369
TAKE A LOOK AT
THE GUY'S PANTS, HUH?

336
00:15:11,411 --> 00:15:13,663
I MEAN, I KNOW YOU TOLD US
TO SHOW EXCITEMENT

337
00:15:13,705 --> 00:15:16,165
BUT DON'T YOU THINK HE WENT
A LITTLE OVERBOARD.

338
00:15:17,542 --> 00:15:18,835
WHAT'S THE MATTER
WITH YOU?

339
00:15:18,877 --> 00:15:19,960
GET OUT OF HERE.

340
00:15:20,002 --> 00:15:21,671
YEAH, TAKE A HIKE,
WET PANTS.

341
00:15:24,048 --> 00:15:25,592
CAN YOU BELIEVE THIS?

342
00:15:25,633 --> 00:15:27,468
WE'RE GOING TO BE
ON THE PLATFORM

343
00:15:27,510 --> 00:15:29,053
FOR THE MILLENNIAL MOMENT.

344
00:15:29,095 --> 00:15:30,179
I KNOW.

345
00:15:30,221 --> 00:15:31,639
HEY, YOU HAVEN'T
BEEN PRACTICING

346
00:15:31,681 --> 00:15:32,682
THE ROUTINE,
HAVE YOU?

347
00:15:32,724 --> 00:15:34,225
NO.

348
00:15:35,685 --> 00:15:37,353
ME, TOO.

349
00:15:37,395 --> 00:15:39,439
HEY, WHEN THE MUSIC
STARTS UP AGAIN

350
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:42,983
I WAS THINKING ABOUT
MAYBE GOING INTO THE
ROBOT, YOU KNOW.

351
00:15:46,571 --> 00:15:48,573
ROSS, I THINK WE SHOULD
STICK TO THE ROUTINE.

352
00:15:48,615 --> 00:15:49,908
WE DON'T WANT
TO LOOK STUPID.

353
00:15:51,785 --> 00:15:52,952
ALL RIGHT, WE'RE BACK.

354
00:15:52,993 --> 00:15:54,621
TEN SECONDS LEFT.
HERE WE GO.

355
00:15:54,662 --> 00:15:55,622
TEN...

356
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:56,623
All:
NINE...

357
00:15:56,664 --> 00:15:57,957
EIGHT...

358
00:15:57,998 --> 00:15:58,999
SEVEN...

359
00:15:59,041 --> 00:16:00,167
Joey:
OKAY...

360
00:16:00,209 --> 00:16:01,628
IT ALL COMES DOWN TO THIS.

361
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:04,464
WHATEVER HAPPENS, HAPPENS.

362
00:16:04,505 --> 00:16:06,925
DESTINY.

363
00:16:06,966 --> 00:16:08,217
THREE...

364
00:16:08,259 --> 00:16:09,302
TWO...

365
00:16:09,343 --> 00:16:10,470
ONE...

366
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:11,095
CUT!

367
00:16:11,137 --> 00:16:12,430
NO!

368
00:16:13,807 --> 00:16:16,476
YEAR!

369
00:16:16,517 --> 00:16:19,312
HAPPY NO YEAR.

370
00:16:21,188 --> 00:16:23,441
HERE'S WHERE WE GO TO
THE LIVE SHOT OF TIMES SQUARE.

371
00:16:23,483 --> 00:16:24,484
THAT'S A WRAP.

372
00:16:34,619 --> 00:16:37,246
( quacking )

373
00:16:37,288 --> 00:16:38,706
HEY, LOOK WHO I FOUND.

374
00:16:38,748 --> 00:16:40,667
OH, HI, GUYS.

375
00:16:40,708 --> 00:16:43,503
YOU KNOW, BIRDS HAVE A VERY GOOD
SENSE OF DIRECTION.

376
00:16:43,544 --> 00:16:45,212
I THOUGHT MAYBE
THEY COULD HELP US FIND

377
00:16:45,254 --> 00:16:46,714
WHERE THE PRESENTS ARE HIDDEN.

378
00:16:46,756 --> 00:16:51,260
YES, IF THE PRESENTS ARE
HIDDEN SOUTH FOR THE WINTER.

379
00:16:51,302 --> 00:16:53,847
OR WE COULD JUST FOLLOW
YOUR CLEVER JOKES.

380
00:16:53,888 --> 00:16:55,849
ANY IDEAS? NO? DIDN'T THINK SO.

381
00:16:55,890 --> 00:16:58,184
COME ON, GUYS.

382
00:16:58,225 --> 00:17:00,144
SHOW US WHERE
THE PRESENTS ARE.

383
00:17:00,186 --> 00:17:03,397
THE DUCK SEEMS TO THINK
THAT MONICA GOT ME GARBAGE.

384
00:17:03,439 --> 00:17:05,608
HMM, I WONDER
WHAT I CAN GET MONICA

385
00:17:05,650 --> 00:17:07,360
THAT'S AS GOOD AS GARBAGE?

386
00:17:07,401 --> 00:17:09,863
HMM, HOW ABOUT MY "AZ"?

387
00:17:11,948 --> 00:17:14,367
( knocking )

388
00:17:14,408 --> 00:17:17,161
HEY, THIS IS HOLLOW.

389
00:17:17,203 --> 00:17:18,204
WHAT?

390
00:17:18,245 --> 00:17:19,622
THIS BENCH, IT'S HOLLOW.

391
00:17:19,664 --> 00:17:21,708
I CAN'T BELIEVE
I NEVER KNEW THAT.

392
00:17:23,668 --> 00:17:25,336
OH! THE PRESENTS!

393
00:17:25,378 --> 00:17:27,213
NO, DON'T LOOK
DIRECTLY AT THEM.

394
00:17:29,215 --> 00:17:30,341
WHAT?

395
00:17:30,383 --> 00:17:32,051
ALL RIGHT, NO,
WE COULD LOOK AT THEM.

396
00:17:32,092 --> 00:17:33,845
OH, THIS ONE'S
FOR ME.

397
00:17:33,887 --> 00:17:35,805
THIS ONE'S FOR CHANDLER.

398
00:17:35,847 --> 00:17:36,806
ALL RIGHT.

399
00:17:36,848 --> 00:17:38,641
AND THE BIG ONE'S
FOR ME.

400
00:17:38,683 --> 00:17:39,851
LET'S OPEN THEM.

401
00:17:39,893 --> 00:17:41,019
OKAY, OKAY.

402
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:42,896
WAIT A MINUTE,
WAIT A MINUTE.

403
00:17:42,937 --> 00:17:44,104
WE CAN'T DO THIS.

404
00:17:44,146 --> 00:17:45,356
WHY?
WHY?

405
00:17:45,398 --> 00:17:47,483
I DON'T WANT TO KNOW
WHAT MONICA GOT ME.

406
00:17:47,525 --> 00:17:50,069
I MEAN, LOOK, I'M SURE
SHE WORKED REALLY HARD

407
00:17:50,110 --> 00:17:52,822
AT GETTING ME A PRESENT
AND WANTING TO SURPRISE ME

408
00:17:52,864 --> 00:17:54,782
AND YOU GUYS ARE GOING
TO RUIN THAT.

409
00:17:54,824 --> 00:17:56,534
LOOK, WE HAVE
TO PUT THESE BACK.

410
00:17:56,576 --> 00:17:58,494
THIS IS NOT WHAT
CHRISTMAS IS ABOUT.

411
00:17:58,536 --> 00:18:00,120
WHATEVER, LINUS.

412
00:18:00,162 --> 00:18:01,956
I'M OPENING MINE.

413
00:18:03,917 --> 00:18:06,711
NOBODY IS OPENING ANYTHING,
OKAY?

414
00:18:06,753 --> 00:18:09,047
I DON'T KNOW
ABOUT YOU GUYS

415
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:11,591
BUT I WANT TO SEE THE LOOK
ON MONICA'S FACE

416
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:13,175
WHEN I GIVE HER
MY PRESENT.

417
00:18:13,217 --> 00:18:16,136
AND I'M SURE SHE WANTS TO SEE
THE LOOK ON MY FACE

418
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:17,555
WHEN I GET MINE.

419
00:18:17,597 --> 00:18:19,933
SO PLEASE, CAN WE JUST...
CAN WE PUT THEM BACK?

420
00:18:19,974 --> 00:18:22,101
WILL YOU GET US BETTER GIFTS?

421
00:18:22,142 --> 00:18:24,520
FINE.

422
00:18:24,562 --> 00:18:26,230
HEY, GUYS.

423
00:18:28,649 --> 00:18:30,818
YOU FOUND THE PRESENTS?

424
00:18:30,860 --> 00:18:33,237
CHANDLER, YOU LET
THEM FIND THE PRESENTS?

425
00:18:33,279 --> 00:18:34,989
GREAT.

426
00:18:35,031 --> 00:18:37,825
DO YOU KNOW HOW LONG IT TOOK ME
TO FIND YOU THAT WATER PURIFIER?

427
00:18:38,868 --> 00:18:40,787
THAT'S WHAT YOU GOT ME?

428
00:18:40,828 --> 00:18:43,163
YES, I SEE WHAT YOU MEAN.
THAT LOOK IS PRICELESS.

429
00:18:49,963 --> 00:18:52,423
HOME SWEET HOME, HUH?

430
00:18:52,465 --> 00:18:55,843
NICE TO GET BACK
TO REALITY.

431
00:18:57,261 --> 00:18:59,472
PLUS, WE KNOW HOW
THE NEW YEAR'S

432
00:18:59,513 --> 00:19:00,640
GOING TO GO OFF.

433
00:19:00,681 --> 00:19:02,475
I GUESS THERE'S NO REASON

434
00:19:02,516 --> 00:19:04,894
FOR ALL THAT Y2K
PANIC, YOU KNOW.

435
00:19:06,687 --> 00:19:08,439
ANYWAY, GOOD NIGHT.

436
00:19:09,398 --> 00:19:10,399
JOEY.

437
00:19:10,441 --> 00:19:11,651
YEAH?

438
00:19:12,819 --> 00:19:14,028
THREE...

439
00:19:14,070 --> 00:19:17,031
TWO... ONE.

440
00:19:24,122 --> 00:19:26,499
HAPPY NEW YEAR.

441
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:28,208
( clearing throat )

442
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:30,210
( mumbling )

443
00:19:30,252 --> 00:19:32,880
WHAT WAS THAT FOR?

444
00:19:32,922 --> 00:19:34,090
I DON'T KNOW.

445
00:19:34,132 --> 00:19:35,842
TONIGHT WHEN THEY
YELLED CUT

446
00:19:35,883 --> 00:19:37,343
AND WE DIDN'T
GET TO KISS

447
00:19:37,384 --> 00:19:39,512
I WAS REALLY, REALLY
DISAPPOINTED.

448
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:40,847
AND I JUST...

449
00:19:40,888 --> 00:19:43,182
I JUST REALLY WANTED
TO KISS YOU.

450
00:19:43,223 --> 00:19:45,852
REALLY?

451
00:19:45,893 --> 00:19:46,978
IN THE MOMENT

452
00:19:47,020 --> 00:19:49,438
I REALLY WANTED
TO KISS YOU, TOO.

453
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:50,564
IN THE MOMENT.

454
00:19:50,606 --> 00:19:51,941
IN THE MOMENT, HUH?

455
00:19:51,983 --> 00:19:53,484
BUT ONLY IN THE MOMENT.

456
00:19:55,111 --> 00:19:56,946
SO, DO YOU...

457
00:19:56,988 --> 00:19:59,740
WANT TO KISS AGAIN?

458
00:19:59,782 --> 00:20:03,870
SURE. NEW YEAR'S EVE
IS ONLY TWO WEEKS AWAY.

459
00:20:03,911 --> 00:20:05,121
CAN YOU WAIT?

460
00:20:05,163 --> 00:20:07,206
NO.

461
00:20:07,247 --> 00:20:10,084
ME NEITHER.

462
00:20:12,628 --> 00:20:16,049
THREE... TWO...

463
00:20:16,090 --> 00:20:17,216
JOEY, YOU DON'T
HAVE TO COUNTDOWN

464
00:20:17,257 --> 00:20:18,258
EVERY TIME WE KISS.

465
00:20:18,926 --> 00:20:19,927
OKAY.

466
00:20:22,262 --> 00:20:24,724
EXCEPT THAT I SORT OF FELT
LIKE I NEEDED

467
00:20:24,765 --> 00:20:26,350
A COUPLE SECONDS
TO GET READY.

468
00:20:50,290 --> 00:20:51,709
WE WERE ON THE PLATFORM

469
00:20:51,751 --> 00:20:54,712
READY TO DANCE THE WORLD
INTO THE NEW MILLENNIUM

470
00:20:54,754 --> 00:20:56,254
AND THE GUY YELLS "CUT."

471
00:20:56,296 --> 00:20:58,799
WAIT A MINUTE,
SO YOU GUYS ARE TELLING ME

472
00:20:58,841 --> 00:21:02,095
THAT YOU ACTUALLY DID
THE ROUTINE FROM EIGHTH GRADE?

473
00:21:02,136 --> 00:21:03,763
YEAH.

474
00:21:03,804 --> 00:21:07,683
BUT OF COURSE WE HAD TO
UPDATE IT A LITTLE BIT.

475
00:21:07,725 --> 00:21:11,478
HEY, BY THE WAY, QUICK THINKING
ABOUT CATCHING ME.

476
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:13,355
YEAH, 'CAUSE I WAS GOING TO SAY

477
00:21:13,397 --> 00:21:14,565
THERE'S NO WAY YOU COULD HAVE
DONE THE END

478
00:21:14,607 --> 00:21:17,401
THE WAY YOU GUYS DID IT
BACK THEN.

479
00:21:17,443 --> 00:21:19,361
WHAT?

480
00:21:19,403 --> 00:21:21,781
WE COULD DO IT.

481
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:24,867
I DON'T KNOW.
YOU WERE A LOT BIGGER...

482
00:21:24,909 --> 00:21:27,078
I MEAN, STRONGER
BACK THEN.

483
00:21:28,370 --> 00:21:30,581
I CAN DO IT, OKAY.

484
00:21:30,623 --> 00:21:33,918
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

485
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:36,837
ONE, TWO, THREE, FOUR, FIVE...

486
00:21:36,879 --> 00:21:39,506
Both:
SIX, SEVEN, EIGHT.

487
00:21:39,548 --> 00:21:42,384
I CAN'T DO IT!

488
00:21:42,426 --> 00:21:46,055
NOW, YOU DO THAT,
YOU'RE ON TV.

